막차 — an original exorcist short (80s Cel Anime style, made with the Lemo-Opuscar style library)

Story and characters
- Original story, characters and dialogue. The mood of Korean urban-occult fiction is the inspiration; no characters, events or
  settings from any existing work are used. Seoul Metro Line 2 is referred to only by real facts (a loop line completed
  1984-05-22; real station names on a generic route diagram); no operator logos, livery or announcement recordings are used.

Picture
- All imagery is generated by code in this folder (Canvas 2D cels and painted plates, a WebGL videotape/CRT pass). No photos,
  no image generation. Engine pieces adapted from the library's 80s Cel Anime demo (cel.js, post.js, fx.js, head80.js → heads.js),
  Lemo-Opuscar (MIT for code).

Music and sound
- Original score composed and synthesized in music/score.py (numpy: FM electric piano and bells, analog arpeggio, slap bass,
  gated-reverb drums, brass stabs, string pads). No samples, no recordings.
- Sound effects and ambience synthesized in mix.py with the library's core/audio/sfx.py and numpy. No recordings.

Voices
- Google Cloud Text-to-Speech, Chirp 3: HD — ko-KR-Chirp3-HD-Kore (서하), ko-KR-Chirp3-HD-Achird (서준),
  ko-KR-Chirp3-HD-Erinome (station announcements), under the user's Google Cloud account and its terms.
- Fish Audio community voice models (free model s2.1-pro-free), under the user's Fish Audio account and its terms:
  "70대 노스님" (a36c3dd96a79431f87072de815559e97) for 무진, "노인" (d7ae98bb52d74c3796208c6d390c5372) for the 1984 driver.
- Speech check: faster-whisper small (MIT) via the library's core/tts/asr_check.py.

